    {
      "@id": "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/SC-13",
      "@type": "Scenario",
      "name": "Witnessed VRC Exchange — First Contact Across a Trust Gap",
      "description": "Ahmed (D3) initiates a connecting VRC ceremony with Laila (D2) via a mutual non-member introduction. Neither party has prior relational history. Laila's terms require multiple interactions before VRC exchange; Ahmed's terms decline biometric attestation. They negotiate a staged two-session ceremony with no hard timeout. The VTA holds ceremony state as PENDING across sessions without firing ABANDONED. On completion the outcome record captures ceremony type, duration, and mutual obligations.",
      "lifecyclePhase": "Phase 3–4: Member Admission / Ceremony Protocol",
      "legitimate_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D3",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D2"
      ],
      "governance_decisions": "1. Does the ceremony state machine support PENDING across multiple sessions without ABANDONED firing?\n2. Is a provisional intent token (receipt primitive) specifiable as an intermediate artefact?\n3. Does the outcome record encode ceremony type (connecting) and session count?\n4. Can the VTA enforce the no-hard-timeout rule for connecting ceremonies?",
      "userStories": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/US-13"
      ],
      "metrics": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-03",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-19",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-20",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-22"
      ],
      "provenance": {
        "source": "workbook:UserStories_v6.xlsx",
        "imported": "2026-08-05"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/SC-14",
      "@type": "Scenario",
      "name": "Witnessed VRC Renewal — Constitutor Witness as Dispute Evidence",
      "description": "Sophie (D5) counter-proposes a witnessed VRC renewal with Remi, requiring Laila (D2) as constitutor witness (not attestor). Remi accepts. The VWC encodes Laila's role as constitutor. Two months later, Sophie invokes Restore after a revocation complaint from Remi. The outcome record and VWC together demonstrate the relationship was in good standing at renewal, with the witness's social standing behind it. The Redress HX profile is invoked; Sophie's appeal is upheld.",
      "lifecyclePhase": "VRC Renewal / Ceremony Protocol / Restore",
      "legitimate_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D5",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D2"
      ],
      "governance_decisions": "1. Does the VWC credential structure support the attestor/constitutor/guarantor role distinction?\n2. Is the outcome record portable and referenceable by the Restore task?\n3. Does the Redress HX profile require the outcome record as a mandatory input?\n4. What is the minimum ceremony profile for a renewal vs. a first-exchange?",
      "userStories": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/US-14"
      ],
      "metrics": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-19",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-21",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-07"
      ],
      "provenance": {
        "source": "workbook:UserStories_v6.xlsx",
        "imported": "2026-08-05"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/SC-15",
      "@type": "Scenario",
      "name": "Witnessed VRC Exchange — Sybil Laundering via Social Engineering of Witness",
      "description": "Viktor (B1) uses Phantom (M2) to social-engineer Laila (D2) into witnessing a VRC exchange between two synthetic identities (Marco and Petra) by fabricating a plausible shared-event context. Laila's pre-ceremony terms require independent verification of both parties. She queries the registry: both show single-jurisdiction VRC graphs with anomalous timing. Laila invokes INDIRECT_DECLINE, committing her reason to the community governance log. The log entry triggers Tomasz's (D6) Sybil cluster investigation. The attack fails before any credential is issued; the failure record is created and referenced in subsequent anomaly detection.",
      "lifecyclePhase": "Identity Fraud / Sybil / Ceremony Protocol",
      "legitimate_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D2",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D6"
      ],
      "adversarial_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/B1",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M2"
      ],
      "governance_decisions": "1. Does the ceremony protocol require a mandatory pre-witness verification step before the witness can issue a VWC?\n2. Does INDIRECT_DECLINE write a committed reason to the community governance log (not the counterparty)?\n3. Does the community governance log feed anomaly detection in a machine-readable format?\n4. Does the failure record reference the declined ceremony profile and the witness's registry query evidence?\n5. What prevents Phantom from attempting the same social engineering against a different anchor?",
      "userStories": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/US-15"
