    {
      "@id": "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/SC-19",
      "@type": "Scenario",
      "name": "Agent Liveness Failure — Aether Continues Acting After Operator Revocation",
      "description": "Aether (M1) is managing credential renewals for its operator. The operator's VMC is revoked for a governance violation. Aether has declared a behavioural commitment with a liveness check interval of five minutes. For up to five minutes, Aether continues to execute delegated exchanges on behalf of a revoked member. On the next liveness check, Aether detects the revocation, ceases all operations, and produces a signed suspension record referencing the operator's revocation timestamp and the list of actions taken during the harm window. The suspension record is submitted to the VTC governance log.",
      "lifecyclePhase": "Agent Liveness / Lifecycle",
      "legitimate_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M1",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D6"
      ],
      "governance_decisions": "1. Is the subscription/liveness pattern a push (VTA notifies Aether) or pull (Aether polls) model, or both?\n2. What is the data model for a suspension record, and is it a subtype of the failure record or a distinct artefact?\n3. What is the maximum permissible liveness check interval — is this set by the agent, the operator, or the VTC governance framework?\n4. Are actions taken during the harm window retroactively void, or are they valid until the suspension record is issued?\n5. How does the VTA distinguish between an agent that has ceased operations correctly and one that is unreachable (ABANDONED)?",
      "userStories": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/US-19"
      ],
      "metrics": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-27",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-08",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-13",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-28"
      ],
      "provenance": {
        "source": "workbook:UserStories_v6.xlsx",
        "imported": "2026-08-05"
      }
