    {
      "@id": "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/SC-20",
      "@type": "Scenario",
      "name": "Behavioural Commitment Enforcement — Phantom Exceeds Its Declared Envelope",
      "description": "Phantom (M2) has registered with a legitimate operator credential and declared a behavioural commitment: maximum 10 credential presentations per hour, interactions limited to VTC members, no ceremony initiations. Phantom begins exceeding these parameters: 400 presentations per hour, ceremony initiations with non-members, parallel policy fuzzing. Each violation is compared against Phantom's signed behavioural commitment. The VTA generates breach records — cryptographically provable deviations from declared parameters — rather than relying solely on statistical anomaly detection. The breach records trigger a Restore task and Phantom's operator credential is suspended pending investigation.",
      "lifecyclePhase": "Behavioural Commitment Enforcement / Security",
      "legitimate_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D6"
      ],
      "adversarial_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M2",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/B1"
      ],
      "governance_decisions": "1. What is the data model for a behavioural commitment, and how is it bound to the agent's DID at registration?\n2. What trust task produces a breach record — is it a subtype of Signal/Capacity or Restore, or a new task?\n3. Is a breach record sufficient to trigger operator credential suspension, or is a governance vote required?\n4. How does a behavioural commitment differ from a policy token — both constrain permitted behaviour?\n5. Can Phantom manipulate its own behavioural commitment declaration to set parameters that permit its intended attack pattern?",
      "userStories": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/US-20"
      ],
      "metrics": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-28",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-08",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-18",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-05"
      ],
      "provenance": {
        "source": "workbook:UserStories_v6.xlsx",
        "imported": "2026-08-05"
      }
