    {
      "@id": "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/SC-21",
      "@type": "Scenario",
      "name": "Ecological Entity as First-Class Party — Sensor Network in a Land-Use Ceremony",
      "description": "A river basin sensor network holds a DID granted by the relevant jurisdiction (analogous to the Whanganui River's legal personhood in New Zealand). A construction company proposes a land-use exchange with the river basin authority. Under the applicable governance framework, the sensor network is a named party in the Exchange — it declares terms (minimum flow rate thresholds must be maintained; no construction within 50m of the river bank), attests to current ecological state via a verifiable sensor credential, and can invoke Restore if the agreement is breached. The ceremony profile requires all five trust tasks to be executed with the sensor network as a named participant alongside the human parties.",
      "lifecyclePhase": "Entangled Systems / Non-Human Entity",
      "legitimate_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D6"
      ],
      "governance_decisions": "1. Is the sensor network's manifest structurally identical to a human member's manifest, or does it require additional fields (sensor calibration lineage, ecological obligation declarations, legal personhood jurisdiction)?\n2. Does the sensor network's terms declaration follow the same Intent Signal protocol as a human party's, or does it require a machine-readable encoding that differs in structure?\n3. Can the sensor network invoke Restore autonomously, or must a human guardian act on its behalf?\n4. Is a non-human entity's DID resolvable via the same DID method as a human member's M-DID, or does it require a distinct DID method for ecological/IoT entities?\n5. How does the dependency map record the sensor network's relationship to its physical sensors — is sensor calibration lineage part of the manifest or a separate provenance record?",
      "userStories": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/US-21"
      ],
      "metrics": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-29",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-15",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-19",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-24"
      ],
      "provenance": {
        "source": "workbook:UserStories_v6.xlsx",
        "imported": "2026-08-05"
      }
