    {
      "@id": "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/SC-24",
      "@type": "Scenario",
      "name": "VTC Dissolution — Winding Down with Full Member Portability",
      "description": "Daniel's VTC passes a governance vote to dissolve. The dissolution protocol requires: (1) all members notified within 24 hours via Signal; (2) all VMCs revoked via Lifecycle Transition; (3) the Community DID deactivated; (4) the tamper-evident governance ledger preserved and transferred to a designated archive; (5) each member issued a portability package containing their VMC (with dissolution record attached), all outcome records from ceremonies they participated in, all VWCs and endorsements, and the signed dissolution record; (6) a historical legitimacy binding — a signed assertion that all credentials issued before the dissolution date were valid at issuance — so other VTCs can verify the historical record.",
      "lifecyclePhase": "VTC Lifecycle / Dissolution",
      "legitimate_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D1",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D5",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D3"
      ],
      "adversarial_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/B2"
      ],
      "governance_decisions": "1. What is the data model for a portability package — what must it contain as a minimum, and what is the maximum retention SLA?\n2. What is the historical legitimacy binding — which trust task produces it, and which primitives underpin it?\n3. How is the governance ledger preserved — is it transferred to a new DID, archived on-chain, or distributed to members?\n4. What happens to in-flight ceremonies at the moment of dissolution announcement — do they complete, fail, or enter a special DISSOLVING terminal state?\n5. Can the Community DID be deactivated while historical legitimacy binding remains verifiable?",
      "userStories": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/US-24"
      ],
      "metrics": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-30",
