    {
      "@id": "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/SC-25",
      "@type": "Scenario",
      "name": "Governance Configuration Failure — VTA Applies Wrong Framework Version to Live Ceremony",
      "description": "A deployment error causes a VTA to apply governance framework version 1.1 (the amended three-VRC threshold) to a ceremony that was AGREED under version 1.0 (the two-VRC threshold). At Level B, the PEP rejects a sub-exchange that was valid under 1.0 but not under 1.1, producing an unexpected FAILED terminal state for a ceremony whose parties did nothing wrong. The failure record must capture the version mismatch in a machine-readable form. The parties invoke Restore. The Restore task must determine whether the failure was a protocol error (PEP applied wrong version), a governance error (version effective date was set incorrectly), or an implementation error (VTA deployment bug).",
      "lifecyclePhase": "Governance Configuration / Security",
      "legitimate_personas": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D5",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/D6"
      ],
      "governance_decisions": "1. Is governance version binding at ceremony AGREED state a mandatory protocol requirement or an implementation recommendation?\n2. What is the data model for a governance version reference in a ceremony profile — must it be a content-addressed hash of the governance document?\n3. Does a version mismatch failure produce a distinct terminal state (INVALID/VERSION_MISMATCH) or does it collapse to FAILED?\n4. What is the Restore pathway for a ceremony that failed due to a governance configuration error — who initiates, who adjudicates, and what is the remediation?\n5. How does the spec prevent a malicious VTA operator from deliberately applying an incorrect governance version to deny a ceremony to targeted members?",
      "userStories": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/US-25"
      ],
      "metrics": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/M-25",
